# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The issue stems from the utilization of tall trees in numerous merkle trees within the BeaconChainProofs library. This could lead to considerable gas consumption during the creation and verification of such trees. The consequence of this vulnerability is that it could hinder the execution of smart contract transactions or make them excessively costly, potentially resulting in the loss of funds or denial of service for users.

## Proof of Concept
There's a possible weakness in the way some trees are set up that could make them vulnerable to attack. These trees are called merkle trees, and the ones in question are the VALIDATOR_TREE_HEIGHT and BALANCE_TREE_HEIGHT. They're set really high - 40 and 38 - which means they could use up a lot of energy when they're built and checked. If someone wanted to be mean, they could create a huge tree that would use up all the energy available and stop other people from doing anything on the network.

